        "original_id": "6a9f75ac-688a-5507-a678-afa530e36a5c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: MGM Grand fire, Winecoff Hotel fire, Dupont Plaza Hotel fire\n- Places: Nevada, Atlanta, Georgia, San Juan, Puerto Rico, Peachtree Street\n- Buildings: Winecoff Hotel\n\nFacts:\n- The 1946 Winecoff Hotel fire in Atlanta killed 119 people.\n- The Winecoff Hotel was located at 176 Peachtree Street in downtown Atlanta, Georgia, United States.\n- The Winecoff Hotel was advertised as \"absolutely fireproof\".\n- The Dupont Plaza Hotel fire in San Juan, Puerto Rico, occurred on December 31, 1986, and killed 97 people.\n- The MGM Grand fire remains the worst disaster in Nevada history.\n- The MGM Grand fire is the third-worst hotel fire in modern U.S. history, after the 1946 Winecoff Hotel fire and the 1986 Dupont Plaza Hotel fire.",
